#Twoweaponing
-------------

  Note: Twoweaponing at Unskilled is a DevTeam deathtrap: -9 to-hit
bonus and -3 damage bonus per weapon, no matter what your skill is with
the weapons individually.  You have been warned.  

  (I think classes restricted in Twoweapon should still be able to
#twoweapon, just as they can use any other weapon they're restricted in.
Permanent -9 to hit and -3 damage per weapon.  I'd like to see a Monk
wearing body armor try that.  Muahahaha!)

  #twoweaponing vs a twohanded weapon:
   - Silver secondary weapon 
     - no two-handed silver weapons.
     - Average +10.5 damage vs silver haters is BIG.
       - e.g. all demons
     - Silver sabers can generally be found.
     - Even a silver dagger or spear at unskilled might be worth it
       - until a silver saber can be found.
   - Strength and blessed bonuses are doubled
     - Strength up to +6.
     - blessed vs certain monsters is +2.5
   - Enchantment damage bonus can be doubled.
     - Requires twice as many blessed scrolls of enchant weapon.
     - Up to +7.
   - Ring of increase damage bonus is doubled.  
     - E.g. a +4 ring of increase damage would have it's effect doubled 
       to +8
   - Skill bonus is about equal

  Thats up to +6 for strength and +7 for enchantment.  That's an extra
+13 right there.  +10.5 and +2.5 for vs silver haters and blessed haters
is another +13.  A best case scenario of +26.  Conservative average of
+18.  No two-handed weapon does as much as +18 damage to begin with,
much less outweigh a good one-handed artifact weapon by that much.

>And is it true that all elven armor
>can go to +7?  Does that include elven boots, mithril coat, elven
>leather helms, and shields?

  Yes, and don't forget cloaks.  Remember, it's safe to enchant at +5,
not +6.  Elven shields are the standout example because their base AC is
2.  Wearing fully enchanted Elven boots, helm, shields, and cloaks gives
8 to 9 more total AC than their counterparts.  (One player recently did
this.)

  This is why elven armor is prized by mad polymorphers.  Elven boots
and cloaks are considered magical armor.  Polymorphing +7 Elven boots
and cloaks gives a chance of getting some other type of magical armor at
+7: CoMR, CoDisp, Helms of Brilliance, Gauntlets of Dexterity, Gauntlets
of Power etc.  That takes a lot of Elven boots/cloaks, polymorphing, and
patience.

